1
00:00:16,544 --> 00:00:20,327
[SPEAKER_01]: So, this is from the Anguttara Nikaya, Book of the Threes.

2
00:00:21,808 --> 00:00:24,050
[SPEAKER_01]: Because there are these three kinds of purity.

3
00:00:24,510 --> 00:00:25,011
[SPEAKER_01]: What three?

4
00:00:25,531 --> 00:00:27,613
[SPEAKER_01]: Purity of body, speech, and mind.

5
00:00:28,573 --> 00:00:29,734
[SPEAKER_01]: And what is purity of body?

6
00:00:30,475 --> 00:00:34,898
[SPEAKER_01]: It is when a bhikkhu abstains from killing living creatures, stealing, and in celibacy.

7
00:00:35,519 --> 00:00:37,040
[SPEAKER_01]: This is called purity of body.

8
00:00:37,861 --> 00:00:40,042
[SPEAKER_01]: And what is purity of speech?

9
00:00:40,062 --> 00:00:43,085
[SPEAKER_01]: It's when a bhikkhu abstains from false, malicious, harsh, and

10
00:00:45,037 --> 00:00:46,278
[SPEAKER_01]: This is called purity of speech.

11
00:00:47,899 --> 00:00:49,080
[SPEAKER_01]: And what is purity of mind?

12
00:00:50,241 --> 00:00:57,086
[SPEAKER_01]: It's when a bhikkhu, when there is sensual desire internally, understands there is sensual desire internally for me.

13
00:00:58,127 --> 00:01:03,971
[SPEAKER_01]: When there is no sensual desire internally, he understands there is no sensual desire internally for me.

14
00:01:04,908 --> 00:01:16,150
[SPEAKER_01]: He understands how un-arisen sensual desire arises, how arisen sensual desire is abandoned, and how abandoned sensual desire doesn't arise again in the future.

15
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:21,491
[SPEAKER_01]: And then it goes on for the other hindrances in the same way.

16
00:01:21,651 --> 00:01:30,873
[SPEAKER_01]: Perversion, second hindrances, second hindrance, indolence and lethargy, then restlessness and anxiety, and also doubt.

17
00:01:32,053 --> 00:01:32,953
[SPEAKER_01]: Then there's also verse,

18
00:01:40,382 --> 00:01:54,648
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, one thing that stands out to me here is concerning the purity of mind.

19
00:01:55,609 --> 00:01:57,469
[SPEAKER_01]: Let's take this first hymn for example.

20
00:01:57,990 --> 00:02:00,051
[SPEAKER_01]: It says, what is purity of mind?

21
00:02:01,531 --> 00:02:08,354
[SPEAKER_01]: When there is desire, sensual desire internally, he understands there is sensual desire internally for me.

22
00:02:09,583 --> 00:02:12,445
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, when there's no sensual desire internally, you understand?

23
00:02:12,465 --> 00:02:14,486
[SPEAKER_01]: There's no sensual desire internally for me.

24
00:02:15,047 --> 00:02:17,908
[SPEAKER_01]: And both are defined here as purity.

25
00:02:19,369 --> 00:02:20,110
[SPEAKER_01]: How is that possible?

26
00:02:20,610 --> 00:02:25,073
[SPEAKER_01]: How can there be purity when somebody understands that there's still sensual desire internally?

27
00:02:25,874 --> 00:02:26,414
[SPEAKER_01]: What would you say?

28
00:02:28,655 --> 00:02:35,620
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, so... That's what I think we sort of...

29
00:02:36,158 --> 00:02:39,679
[SPEAKER_00]: I touched on that in some of the previous talks about patient endurance and so on.

30
00:02:40,759 --> 00:02:56,024
[SPEAKER_00]: The recognition that underlies that principle is that, fundamentally, impurity or defilement arises on account of your choices.

31
00:02:57,145 --> 00:02:58,565
[SPEAKER_00]: It never arises by accident.

32
00:02:59,805 --> 00:03:04,707
[SPEAKER_00]: And the five hindrances are, technically, something that isn't

33
00:03:06,394 --> 00:03:08,955
[SPEAKER_00]: Up to you, whether they're there or not.

34
00:03:08,995 --> 00:03:20,318
[SPEAKER_00]: If you, for example, if you haven't been in seclusion, even for an anahant, those things would still be there.

35
00:03:20,338 --> 00:03:20,939
[SPEAKER_01]: Those hindrances.

36
00:03:20,979 --> 00:03:21,199
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

37
00:03:21,399 --> 00:03:31,482
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's why some of the suttas, for example, would say... well, that's... it's not obviously the same thing, because when craving is not there, you cannot say it's the same thing anymore.

38
00:03:31,622 --> 00:03:31,882
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

39
00:03:32,142 --> 00:03:34,083
[SPEAKER_00]: But the, let's say, the shape... the shape

40
00:03:35,943 --> 00:03:45,366
[SPEAKER_00]: The shell of those things would be essentially the same thing, kind of like dried up, but it's the same thing.

41
00:03:46,406 --> 00:03:53,328
[SPEAKER_00]: Sometimes the suttas would say like a tree with the root cut off, but like the tree is still there, standing, but dead.

42
00:03:54,068 --> 00:04:02,071
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the point is that even for them, like another sutta would, for example, say the Narahant is not

43
00:04:04,809 --> 00:04:21,680
[SPEAKER_00]: Detached externally from things like fame, gain, popularity, and sort of worldly engagements that are not against the precepts, but, you know, happen as a result of circumstance or whatever, they will lose their pleasant abiding here and now.

44
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:28,885
[SPEAKER_00]: And even in some cases, which is a another way of saying they will lose their abiding free from these five things.

45
00:04:30,786 --> 00:04:51,896
[SPEAKER_00]: In many cases, stories in the suttas, the Buddha would, like, refuse to be visited by people who wanted to just bring offerings to, kind of, just without really any interest in the dhamma, because he knew that that would result in unnecessary engagements that would basically make his mind

46
00:04:52,616 --> 00:05:00,739
[SPEAKER_00]: It's more liable to those things and it's not that, you know, it might sound then as if, oh, he was craving to maintain his samādhi or something.

47
00:05:01,139 --> 00:05:11,483
[SPEAKER_00]: And it says there, whoever cannot get at ease, at will, that pleasure of renunciation, they would agree to these things, but I won't.

48
00:05:12,144 --> 00:05:14,965
[SPEAKER_00]: And that sounds like, oh, he's attached to his samādhi or something.

49
00:05:15,725 --> 00:05:17,546
[SPEAKER_00]: But the point is, like, no.

50
00:05:19,932 --> 00:05:28,355
[SPEAKER_00]: In itself, the principle of preferring pleasure and avoiding pain is something that's embedded into the aggregates.

51
00:05:28,675 --> 00:05:30,416
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not, in and of itself, craving.

52
00:05:31,096 --> 00:05:33,777
[SPEAKER_00]: Craving is another layer that's added to that.

53
00:05:33,817 --> 00:05:34,618
[SPEAKER_00]: Let's put it that way.

54
00:05:35,158 --> 00:05:42,961
[SPEAKER_00]: So, the point here, then, is that, yes, inevitably, even, like, no matter how diligent you are, how

55
00:05:44,163 --> 00:05:52,406
[SPEAKER_00]: perfectly committed to the to the path you are, there will be times when those things will be there in your mind.

56
00:05:53,067 --> 00:06:02,090
[SPEAKER_00]: And if it were a matter of not having those things in order to be pure, it would mean that basically you could lose your arahantship.

57
00:06:02,610 --> 00:06:03,451
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's impossible.

58
00:06:03,651 --> 00:06:08,112
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what I just mentioned that says an arahant will lose their pleasant abidings.

59
00:06:08,693 --> 00:06:12,414
[SPEAKER_00]: It says also the unshakable liberation of mind

60
00:06:13,079 --> 00:06:14,060
[SPEAKER_00]: That cannot be lost.

61
00:06:14,340 --> 00:06:15,581
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why it's called unshakable.

62
00:06:16,122 --> 00:06:17,984
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's what this is describing.

63
00:06:18,144 --> 00:06:33,038
[SPEAKER_00]: Meaning, the understanding of your mind, even when it is in such a state, means that you will be unable to make choices on account of sensual desire, on account of ill will.

64
00:06:33,318 --> 00:06:37,282
[SPEAKER_00]: And because of that, I mean, technically, you use, again,

65
00:06:39,755 --> 00:06:44,758
[SPEAKER_00]: In an ordinary person, those states are made what they are, because they act out of them.

66
00:06:45,239 --> 00:06:50,422
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why then, when the acting out has been completely destroyed, you can't call them hindrances anymore.

67
00:06:51,082 --> 00:06:55,345
[SPEAKER_00]: But, in and of itself, like, it's kind of the same thing.

68
00:06:55,365 --> 00:07:03,390
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's why it requires nuance and caveats need to be made, because otherwise people think also you're saying an arahant still has unwholesome states.

69
00:07:04,091 --> 00:07:07,453
[SPEAKER_00]: But the thing is now, the state, like the whole point,

70
00:07:08,598 --> 00:07:13,199
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, this is exactly what a sotāpanna understands, and that's why they're able to cultivate the path.

71
00:07:13,739 --> 00:07:24,381
[SPEAKER_00]: As a sotāpanna says, he understands that the defilements are gratuitous, like they're kind of... he says they flow in on the mind.

72
00:07:25,301 --> 00:07:33,942
[SPEAKER_00]: And so, it means states and your actions on account of it, and your intentions on account of it, are two separate things.

73
00:07:34,143 --> 00:07:34,363
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

74
00:07:35,163 --> 00:07:36,363
[SPEAKER_00]: Which is the same thing as saying

75
00:07:37,416 --> 00:07:40,317
[SPEAKER_00]: Unpleasant feeling is one thing, and craving is another thing.

76
00:07:40,417 --> 00:07:43,358
[SPEAKER_00]: And it sounds kind of... Oh, yeah, of course, that makes sense.

77
00:07:43,718 --> 00:07:47,459
[SPEAKER_00]: But seeing that concretely, means seeing the Four Noble Truths.

78
00:07:47,639 --> 00:07:48,579
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's the same with this.

79
00:07:49,119 --> 00:07:58,282
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, seeing how you can have these mental states, without there being any craving, if you understand that, that would already be stream entry.

80
00:07:58,802 --> 00:08:05,504
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why, in the Satipaṭṭhāna Sutta as well, it says, in the mind contemplation section, it says,

81
00:08:06,418 --> 00:08:14,444
[SPEAKER_00]: How does a bhikkhu abide, maintain the perspective of the mind, simultaneously with the mind?

82
00:08:15,144 --> 00:08:21,828
[SPEAKER_00]: It doesn't say, when he has a passionate mind, he gets rid of it, or he stops thinking.

83
00:08:22,129 --> 00:08:26,091
[SPEAKER_00]: It says, he knows a passionate mind as a passionate mind.

84
00:08:26,291 --> 00:08:29,574
[SPEAKER_00]: He knows an averse mind as an averse mind, and so on.

85
00:08:29,614 --> 00:08:32,115
[SPEAKER_00]: It lists all these possibilities and permutations.

86
00:08:32,175 --> 00:08:34,817
[SPEAKER_00]: In the end, it says, one who abides like this,

87
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:57,591
[SPEAKER_00]: So, of course, if you continue abiding in that way, with this recognition of passionate mind as passionate mind and so on, you're essentially... that's what's taking your mind away from that.

88
00:08:57,991 --> 00:09:05,055
[SPEAKER_00]: But that's, in and of itself, it's not that it's unwholesome for those states to be there, if there's no ignorance.

89
00:09:05,115 --> 00:09:07,377
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why, as it is to say, an arahant is

90
00:09:07,984 --> 00:09:11,930
[SPEAKER_00]: In other words, they don't even need to practice samādhi anymore.

91
00:09:12,771 --> 00:09:16,956
[SPEAKER_00]: But, yes, if... and that's what a trainee has to do.

92
00:09:17,657 --> 00:09:24,687
[SPEAKER_00]: They have to maintain perspective of these states and genuinely try to free their mind from these states, so that they can

93
00:09:25,504 --> 00:09:45,819
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, so that is part of the understanding of how an arisen sensual desire arises and how an arisen sensual desire is abandoned.

94
00:09:45,899 --> 00:09:46,800
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the difference there.

95
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:53,105
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, and obviously, then, the thing to clarify is, like, you will never be able to

96
00:09:54,152 --> 00:10:09,062
[SPEAKER_00]: If you don't have that knowledge and that type of purity, if you haven't beforehand cultivated the freedom from, like completely, freedom from sensual desire, freedom from aversion, freedom from these things, which is always temporary...

97
00:10:09,082 --> 00:10:10,163
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is Sattva Samādhi.

98
00:10:10,223 --> 00:10:10,463
[SPEAKER_01]: Yes.

99
00:10:10,723 --> 00:10:23,112
[SPEAKER_00]: If you haven't practiced that, like, practicing that is what enables you to, like, when you come back to the normal, sort of, like, dealing with stuff and movement of the mind and so on,

100
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:31,912
[SPEAKER_00]: All of the wrong assumptions and ignorance and craving can't be there, even though you went back to to baseline, quote-unquote.

101
00:10:33,574 --> 00:10:33,794
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

102
00:10:34,115 --> 00:10:37,920
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, there is some ambiguity here about the words mental.

103
00:10:44,966 --> 00:10:51,091
[SPEAKER_01]: And it talks about sensuality and the other hindrances internally, but then you start it out by saying, no, no, hindrances is when we act out.

104
00:10:51,772 --> 00:10:57,076
[SPEAKER_01]: But we should clear up that acting out is by body, by speech, and by mind.

105
00:10:57,356 --> 00:10:57,536
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

106
00:10:57,736 --> 00:11:01,880
[SPEAKER_01]: So, there is also a mental acting out, which is on the level of

107
00:11:02,967 --> 00:11:07,429
