[SPEAKER_00]: In your control, at some point, you will have to abandon seclusion, and that means you will lose your samādhi, because, as it is said, the first jhāna is a cessation of speech.

119
00:12:53,755 --> 00:12:55,736
[SPEAKER_00]: So, as soon as you start speaking, you're back to...

120
00:12:55,996 --> 00:12:56,196
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

121
00:12:56,216 --> 00:13:01,699
[SPEAKER_00]: ...back to the normal kind of state, and that's why restraining speech is so important as well.

122
00:13:02,359 --> 00:13:03,920
[SPEAKER_00]: But, eh...

123
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:09,302
[SPEAKER_00]: So, because it's always connected with your intention, eh...

124
00:13:10,735 --> 00:13:13,676
[SPEAKER_00]: Like I said before, it is always in your control.

125
00:13:13,716 --> 00:13:24,220
[SPEAKER_00]: But the problem is, there's this natural assumption, again, because of not being able to clearly see that difference between citta and mano, which is...

126
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:30,482
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, if you can see that, that's already... essentially, that is the right view.

127
00:13:31,122 --> 00:13:35,223
[SPEAKER_00]: If you can see that... because, by the way, that's how you see wholesome and unwholesome.

128
00:13:35,744 --> 00:13:39,285
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, you know, most of people would just assume, if I have

129
00:13:39,943 --> 00:13:53,871
