151
00:16:03,140 --> 00:16:05,741
[SPEAKER_00]: If there is... well, actually, that's a good point.

152
00:16:05,841 --> 00:16:27,866
[SPEAKER_00]: The suttas always talk about abandoning unwholesome thoughts, vitakka, and there's a whole... there's these two famous suttas in the Majjhima Nikāya, Majjhima Nikāya 19, Majjhima Nikāya 20, where it talks about, oh, the monk is practicing diligently and then sensual thoughts, averse thoughts arise, and then he gets rid of them, obliterates them, destroys them.

153
00:16:28,506 --> 00:16:31,727
[SPEAKER_00]: And see, because people don't see that distinction between mano and citta,

154
00:16:32,726 --> 00:16:36,469
[SPEAKER_00]: What they're really doing, they're not just stopping at the threshold of their intention.

155
00:16:36,729 --> 00:16:40,792
[SPEAKER_00]: They're going further, and they're trying to destroy the entire citta as well.

156
00:16:41,032 --> 00:16:49,138
[SPEAKER_00]: They don't see... Like, again, to give the example of body and speech, they're not just choosing not to take the object, they're cutting their hands off.

157
00:16:49,458 --> 00:16:53,841
[SPEAKER_00]: And, obviously, they don't recognize that because it's a very subtle kind of...

158
00:16:54,802 --> 00:16:55,262
[SPEAKER_00]: Distinction.

159
00:16:55,282 --> 00:16:55,803
[SPEAKER_00]: Distinction.

160
00:16:56,403 --> 00:16:57,324
[SPEAKER_00]: But, eh...

161
00:16:59,198 --> 00:17:17,721
[SPEAKER_00]: So, only when you're able to see that division, completely kind of a irreconcilable division, the division between mano and citta, between your intention and that internal environment that pressures you to intend, only when you can see that division, you're able to actually purify your mind.

162
00:17:17,921 --> 00:17:23,722
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why, like... Yeah, but to purify mind, which is to purify citta.

163
00:17:24,102 --> 00:17:24,802
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah, well, both.

164
00:17:25,002 --> 00:17:28,003
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, you you're able to... Because, see, if you don't see,

165
00:17:29,703 --> 00:17:33,987
[SPEAKER_00]: This distinction, that's why the suttas say you cannot purify your mind accidentally.

166
00:17:34,267 --> 00:17:36,789
[SPEAKER_00]: Not like suddenly something happened and my mind is pure.

167
00:17:37,229 --> 00:17:37,790
[SPEAKER_00]: Either of them.

168
00:17:38,330 --> 00:17:38,531
[SPEAKER_00]: Yeah.

169
00:17:38,771 --> 00:17:39,832
[SPEAKER_00]: Whether it's mano or citta.

170
00:17:39,912 --> 00:17:41,934
